","Child 7370 AC1: 'represented only by the approved removed-input/tombstone behavior'","Dependency: 7370 depends_on 8ca7, so 7370 must implement per the ADR 8ca7 records","container pairing: parent + 1a63-056e-98b9-4ab7/7370-0274-9f80-437d/8ca7-28c5-c5c4-4f32"],"finding":"Children 8ca7 and 7370 hold directly conflicting assumptions about the removal mechanism, and both contradict the parent. The parent mandates fail-loud `error` tombstones ('Replace each `_permanent` row with an `_tomb` entry at `error` behavior'; AC2 'represented only by an `error` tombstone'). Child 7370 agrees (AC1 'the approved removed-input/tombstone behavior'). But child 8ca7's ADR mandates the OPPOSITE: 'follow-on work must remove the alias declarations and active parsing/warning paths, not convert these aliases to fail-loud tombstones' and AC3 'removes alias declarations and active parsing/warning paths rather than ... converting them into fail-loud tombstones.' Since 7370 depends on 8ca7 and must follow the ADR it records, the two children cannot both satisfy their acceptance criteria, and neither aligns cleanly with the parent's tombstone mandate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4540652f0160fb45","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 8ca7-28c5-c5c4-4f32 (vs child 7370-0274-9f80-437d and parent)","norm_id":"n8a2f389ecba6c393","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Pick one policy. If fail-loud error tombstones are intended (per parent AC2), rewrite 8ca7's Context/AC3 to record tombstone conversion rather than clean removal. If clean removal is intended (per the Janitor approval as 8ca7 reads it), rewrite parent AC2 and 7370 AC1 to require deletion of the declarations, not an `error` tombstone.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_wo